# C++ data member naming

Do **not** use a trailing underscore suffix on class/struct data members.

```cpp
// Bad
class Foo {
    int count_ = 0;
    Array<Item> items_{};
};

// Good
class Foo {
    int count = 0;
    Array<Item> items{};
};
```

## Guidelines

- Name members in plain camelCase (or match the surrounding type), without a `_` suffix.
- When a constructor parameter has the same name as a member, qualify the member with `this->` in the initializer list and body.
- When a local variable would shadow a member, rename the local (e.g. `listUp`, `object`) instead of suffixing the member.
- Trailing underscores on **private helper methods** (e.g. `ClipValid_`) are acceptable if already used in that file; do not add new ones unless matching existing local style.
